{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.coCasimir_sector_contributes_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.coCasimir_sector_contributes_zero","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L155-L167","doc":"**The Frobenius co-Casimir sector is invariant, and the reason is arity.**\nModelled with `Y = ℕ × R` for the pair `(n, q)`: whatever `G` computes from the\nblock data, the generator sign flip leaves `(n, q)` alone, so the term drops out\nof the split. Both mirror isobars sit at `A = 3`, hence at the same `n`, so it\ncancels between them exactly rather than approximately.\n\nThis supplies **one** of the two premises\n`rem:isospin-mass-split-em-localisation` was missing. The other, the trace\ntower, is false at the substrate — `QOU.MassTheory.TraceSignFlipRegime`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.factoringSector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.factoringSector","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L148-L153","doc":"The sector built from such a factorisation, as an `InvariantSector` — so it\ncan be dropped straight into the list `split_sum_eq_split_remainder` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split_comp_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split_comp_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L139-L146","doc":"**A sector that factors through an `ι`-invariant of the state contributes\nzero to the split.** More useful in practice than checking invariance directly,\nbecause it is usually obvious *by arity* that a sector cannot see what `ι`\nmoves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.omitted_sector_breaks_localisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.omitted_sector_breaks_localisation","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L106-L121","doc":"**The enumeration is load-bearing, not bookkeeping.** If a sector that is\n*not* invariant is left out of the list, the localisation conclusion is false:\nhere the remainder `G` has zero split, so the argument would report \"the split is\nentirely `G`'s, hence zero\", while the true split is `2`.\n\nConcretely `ι = (· * -1)` on `ℤ`, the omitted sector is the identity, and `G` is\nzero. This is why point 2 above matters: an unproved invariance is\nindistinguishable, to this argument, from an omitted sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split_sum_eq_split_remainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split_sum_eq_split_remainder","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L87-L104","doc":"**Localisation, stated with its enumeration explicit.** If the mass\nfunctional decomposes as a sum over a *given list* of invariant sectors plus a\nremainder `G`, then the split is the split of `G` alone.\n\nThe list is the hypothesis. Read `ss` as \"the trace tower, the co-Casimir, the\nchirality and the shell correction\" and `G` as \"the Coulomb term\", and this is\nthe remark's argument — with the two things it assumes now visible in the\nstatement rather than in the prose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split_invariantSector_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split_invariantSector_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**An invariant sector contributes exactly zero to the split.** The valid core\nof every localisation argument of this shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector.invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector.invariant","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Its invariance under `ι` — the premise that must be *proved* per sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector.F","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The sector's contribution to the mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector.mk","kind":"ctor","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.InvariantSector","kind":"structure","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L72-L79","doc":"A **sector** of the mass functional, bundled with the invariance claim that\nmakes it drop out of the split. Bundling is deliberate: an unbundled `F` with the\ninvariance asserted in prose is exactly the failure mode this file is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InvolutionSelectionRule.split","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InvolutionSelectionRule.lean#L67-L70","doc":"The **`ι`-split** of a functional: its value on a state minus its value on\nthe involuted state. For `ι` the isospin mirror this is `m(³H) − m(³He)`; for\n`ι` the generator sign-flip it is the proton/neutron difference. ","signatureChunk":0}]}